Amazing concept, but theres a lack of depth


30 Nov 2020 15:05






This is an interesting concept but I feel like the execution wasn't the best. First of all, I think there's just not enough detail put into the containment procedures and revision. How the Foundation tracks the movements of the object could be added, as well as more specifics to what  means. If it's unpredictable, say so. In the incident report, I would also specify what kind of aircraft the Foundation used.

Secondly, I would also add a bit more depth or lore to this SCP in general. I think it needs more flavor, for instance, the article has no censorship or redactions whatsoever. I think more detail about the known origins of the SCPs referenced would add a lot of interesting concepts and discussion points.

Overall, I think this is is a very good concept for an SCP. The issue is that the article doesn't give it the interesting points that would make it interesting to read and discuss.







