I agree but theres one more problem I saw.


30 Nov 2020 15:58






I mostly agree with what morsom said, you're writing an in depth SCP article. Also, few more things, A: In the beginning it said that the UFO was Euclid. Since it was  by the foundation it should be Keter, remember Keter doesn't mean it has to be dangerous. Also, you need to make it clear which revision came first. For example in the 106 containment revision it says this is the most recent revision of containment. In other words include at the top of the revision whatever the previous revision would have been. Also it wouldn't hurt to, when the foundation is aware the grey thing is (kind of) separate from the aircraft designate it SCP-5422-1





